126
00:08:09.435 --> 00:08:15.942
Design the limiter service: rule configuration, headers, observability, and the tiers where limits apply.

127
00:08:17.292 --> 00:08:18.167
Part 2.

128
00:08:18.447 --> 00:08:20.345
Core Concepts, Beginner to Deep.

129
00:08:21.595 --> 00:08:24.219
Intuition: turnstiles with different jobs.

130
00:08:24.499 --> 00:08:39.945
A stadium has turnstiles at each gate (per-node limits), a total capacity (a global limit), a rule of four tickets per buyer (per-customer quota), and guards watching for touts buying hundreds of tickets through many friends (abuse detection).

131
00:08:40.225 --> 00:08:44.235
They all limit rate, but they answer different questions and fail differently.

132
00:08:44.515 --> 00:08:51.022
A turnstile jam at one gate shouldn't close the stadium; a broken ticket scanner shouldn't let the touts in free.

133
00:08:52.372 --> 00:08:53.332
Requirements.

134
00:08:53.612 --> 00:08:54.465
Functional.

135
00:08:54.745 --> 00:09:04.900
Evaluate a request against one or more rules (key, algorithm, rate, burst, window) and return allow or deny plus remaining quota and retry-after.

136
00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:09.745
Rules configured per route, per client class, per partner, without redeploying.

137
00:09:10.025 --> 00:09:16.788
Support rate limits (per second or minute), quotas (per day per month) and budgets (per destination range per hour).

138
00:09:17.068 --> 00:09:21.783
Shadow mode: evaluate new rules and log what they would do, without enforcing.

139
00:09:23.133 --> 00:09:24.242
Non-functional.

140
00:09:24.522 --> 00:09:33.802
Latency: under 1 ms p99 added at the gateway, and never a network round-trip per request on hot paths if avoidable (L2).

141
00:09:34.082 --> 00:09:34.829
Scale:

142
00:09:35.109 --> 00:09:40.890
150k req per second at the gateway at sale peaks; 10M+ active keys.

143
00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:45.607
Accuracy: contracts within a few percent; fraud budgets as hard caps.

144
00:09:45.887 --> 00:09:53.482
Availability: the limiter must never be the reason the platform is down; failure behaviour is explicit per rule (L4).

145
00:09:53.762 --> 00:09:56.663
Multi-region: two regions, active-active.

146
00:09:58.013 --> 00:09:59.059
Estimation.

147
00:09:59.339 --> 00:10:00.704
