154
00:10:29.736 --> 00:10:31.165
State with exact logs:

155
00:10:31.445 --> 00:10:37.568
10M times ~1 KB about ~10 GB, and write amplification per request.

156
00:10:37.848 --> 00:10:39.149
Central store load:

157
00:10:39.429 --> 00:10:50.971
450k Lua calls per second, several Redis shards, ~20 to 40 µs each on localhost (L2), 0.5 to 1 ms across AZs.

158
00:10:51.251 --> 00:10:57.779
OTP sends: ~120k or hour normal; attack traffic of the same order (L3).

159
00:10:59.129 --> 00:11:00.878
The estimates point at the design.

160
00:11:01.158 --> 00:11:04.401
GCRA state is small, so storage is not the problem.

161
00:11:04.681 --> 00:11:20.425
One store call per rule per request is expensive at 450k per second and across AZs, so hot-path limits should be local or leased (L2), and exact central checks reserved for low-volume, high-value rules like OTP.

162
00:11:21.775 --> 00:11:24.313
