236
00:14:58.891 --> 00:15:12.161
GCRA (Generic Cell Rate Algorithm, from ATM networks) stores one number per key: the theoretical arrival time (TAT) of the next request if the client sent at exactly the allowed rate.

237
00:15:12.441 --> 00:15:16.835
With emission interval T = 1 or rate and burst tolerance τ:

238
00:15:18.185 --> 00:15:29.001
On screen: newtat = max(tat, now) + T. if newtat - now τ + T, then deny (retry after newtat - T - τ - now). else, then allow, tat = newtat.

239
00:15:31.851 --> 00:15:34.497
It is mathematically a token bucket (L1:

240
00:15:34.777 --> 00:15:41.198
0 of 2.2M decisions differ), with one integer of state and a natural retry-after.

241
00:15:41.478 --> 00:15:44.422
It is what redis-cell and several gateways implement.

242
00:15:44.702 --> 00:15:46.921
Sliding-window counters are approximate.

243
00:15:47.201 --> 00:15:52.321
The weighted two-window estimate assumes the previous window's requests were evenly spread.

244
00:15:52.601 --> 00:15:57.977
Ch 18's single-burst test hid the error; L1's bursty traffic exposed it:

245
00:15:58.257 --> 00:16:15.110
4.3% of decisions differed from the exact log (73,704 extra allows, 22,468 extra denials), and a key reached 108 in a true 60-second span against a limit of 60.

246
00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:19.230
That's better than the fixed window's 120, but not a hard cap.

247
00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:21.963
Use them where roughly N per window is enough.

248
00:16:23.313 --> 00:16:26.705
Exact logs are the only hard at most N in any window.

249
00:16:26.985 --> 00:16:32.745
Use them where that matters and volume is low, OTP sends per phone, with short TTLs.

250
00:16:34.095 --> 00:16:36.762
Enforcing a global limit across many nodes.

251
00:16:37.042 --> 00:16:48.605
L2 enforced one partner's 1,000 req per second contract from 8 gateway nodes, with the partner sending 900 req per second skewed 60% onto node 0:

252
00:16:49.955 --> 00:16:51.320
Here is a quick table:

253
00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:59.643
Strategy, and In-contract requests rejected, and Redis calls per request, and Over the limit (2,000 req per second offered).

254
00:16:59.923 --> 00:17:02.803
Local only (limit ÷ 8 per node).

255
00:17:03.083 --> 00:17:04.960
