316
00:20:45.431 --> 00:20:55.415
Traffic between regions moves, failovers, DNS changes, a partner's own routing, so a static split refuses in-contract traffic exactly when it moves.

317
00:20:55.695 --> 00:21:03.737
Rebalancing shares by recent demand keeps both properties, with only periodic, asynchronous exchange of counts between regions.

318
00:21:04.017 --> 00:21:10.716
A single central limiter is exact until the regions partition, and then it must either over-admit or fail.

319
00:21:10.996 --> 00:21:20.340
Most platforms accept approximate global limits (a few percent) for contracts, and keep hard fraud budgets per region with conservative shares.

320
00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:22.927
