00:27:39.066 --> 00:27:42.437
Security or fraud, SRE, Partner engineering.

430
00:27:42.717 --> 00:27:57.543
Context, v1 limited OTPs per IP (locked out CGNAT customers), missed an SMS-pumping attack, enforced partner contracts as per-node splits, failed closed on a Redis failover, and didn't pace vendor egress.

431
00:27:58.893 --> 00:28:21.080
Decision, Rules as versioned data with shadow mode; GCRA state in regional Redis; leased tokens for high-volume limits, exact central checks for fraud controls; destination-range budgets and attestation for OTP; demand-based cross-region rebalancing for contracts; per-rule failure mode with local fallback; egress shaping for vendors.

432
00:28:22.430 --> 00:28:48.478
Related ADRs, ADR-250 GCRA as the default algorithm, exact log only for OTP-per-phone (L1); ADR-251 Adaptive token leasing at the gateway (L2); ADR-252 OTP keys: phone + destination-range budgets + attestation or challenge; IP limits loose and ASN-based (L3); ADR-253 Cross-region share rebalancing

433
00:28:48.758 --> 00:29:08.662
every 10 s (L4); ADR-254 Failure mode declared per rule; local fallback for fraud budgets (L4); ADR-255 Shadow mode mandatory before enforcement; ADR-256 Vendor egress via leaky-bucket shaper with OTP priority.

434
00:29:08.942 --> 00:29:09.902
Requirements.

435
00:29:10.182 --> 00:29:17.521
R1 Added latency under 1 ms p99 at the gateway at 150k req per second.

436
00:29:18.871 --> 00:29:26.444
R2 Partner contracts enforced within 2% globally; no in-contract rejections when traffic moves between regions.

437
00:29:26.724 --> 00:29:37.839
R3 SMS-pumping cost under 5,000 rupees per day at attack volumes seen so far; real-user OTP denial under 0.05%.

438
00:29:38.119 --> 00:29:42.855
R4 No platform outage caused by the limiter's store; failure mode per rule.

439
00:29:43.135 --> 00:29:45.823
R5 Vendor TPS never exceeded.

440
00:29:46.103 --> 00:29:47.511
Decisions in detail.

441
00:29:48.861 --> 00:29:50.951
State (ADR-250).

442
00:29:51.231 --> 00:30:00.639
GCRA with TAT in microseconds, PX expiry of burst + 1 s; OTP-per-phone as a sorted set with 1 h TTL.

443
00:30:00.919 --> 00:30:03.565
Enforcement (ADR-251).

444
00:30:03.845 --> 00:30:13.253
Leases of ~50 ms of each node's rate (1 to 50 tokens), 100 ms expiry, give-back on expiry, denial caching.

445
00:30:13.533 --> 00:30:15.495
OTP (ADR-252).

446
00:30:15.775 --> 00:30:25.973
Range budgets = 3x the 28-day hourly baseline per range, a per-country and a global international budget; attestation failure, then challenge.

447
00:30:26.253 --> 00:30:28.834
Regions (ADR-253).

448
00:30:29.114 --> 00:30:34.447
Each region publishes per-key demand every 10 s; shares recomputed proportionally.

449
00:30:35.797 --> 00:30:38.315
Failure (ADR-254).

450
00:30:38.595 --> 00:30:46.168
Limiter calls time out at 5 ms; breaker; fallback shares = budget ÷ nodes times 3; alert.

451
00:30:46.448 --> 00:30:49.008
Rollout (ADR-255).

452
00:30:49.288 --> 00:30:54.877
Every new rule spends ≥7 days in shadow with a false-positive review.

453
00:30:55.157 --> 00:30:56.181
Consequences.

454
00:30:56.461 --> 00:31:03.736
More moving parts than a single Redis token bucket: rule configuration, leasing logic and fallback shares to test.

455
00:31:04.016 --> 00:31:06.363
Contracts are approximate by a few percent.

456
00:31:06.643 --> 00:31:10.611
Fraud budgets need tuning and on-call attention during campaigns.

457
00:31:10.891 --> 00:31:19.189
In return: no locked-out carriers, attack cost bounded, partners served within contract, and a limiter that can't take the platform down.

